Miscellaneous bits of documentation that don't really fit anywhere else

@namespace noConflict

**This is only available when Maplair is not imported as a module!**

This method restores the `L` global variable to the original value
it had before Maplair inclusion, and returns the real Maplair
namespace so you can put it elsewhere, like this:


```html
<script src='libs/l.js'>
<!-- L points to some other library -->

<script src='maplair.js'>
<!-- you include Maplair, it replaces the L variable to Maplair namespace -->

<script>
const Maplair = L.noConflict();
// now L points to that other library again, and you can use Maplair.Map etc.
</script>
```

@namespace version

A constant that represents the Maplair version in use.

```js
import { version } from 'maplair';

console.log(version); // contains "2.0.0" (or whatever version is currently in use)
```
